# tools/q/qa_report_card_witness.rish -- quality assurance, as a grade a writer can aim at.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. This tree measured its prose one way: the share of sentences carrying a negative,
# held at or under 20% for a Door document. That number is true and it is also backwards. A reader
# told to hold "20% negative" is being told what the page failed to avoid, and a writer aiming at it
# is aiming at a ceiling rather than at a standard. Read the same measurement the other way up --
# 100 minus that share -- and 20% becomes 80, a B, which is a grade a person has known since school
# and can aim at without translating. Keaton asked for exactly that flip on 20260824, and for the
# grade to reach past prose to code comments and to design.
#
# WHAT A REPORT CARD IS. Four readings of one artifact, each 0 to 100, meaned into one grade.
#   Register  counted   100 minus the negative-sentence share, the same reading prose_register
#                       gates, lifted from that scan rather than copied beside it -- floor and all,
#                       so a page too short to carry a share has it reported rather than scored.
#   Reach     counted   Flesch-Kincaid grade and cross-references per hundred words, against the
#                       budget its setting carries -- unless the page declares itself an index AND
#                       measures like one, where the density is reported rather than scored.
#   Truth     half      counted: every relative link resolved as written, root-relative, or by the
#                       fold rule. Judged: whether a behavioral claim is still honestly true.
#   Service   judged    whether the artifact helps the work actually in front of us, read against
#                       construction/ITINERARY.md. The tool prints the inputs and stops there.
#
# Truth is a gate rather than a quarter: below 60 the whole card reads F, because a page whose
# claims have gone false costs a reader more than an absent page. Honesty first, written into the
# arithmetic rather than left to a habit.
#
# FOUR READINGS THAT LEARNED AN HONEST DENOMINATOR, 20260825. A meter that instructs a repair which
# would make the artifact worse is the thing to fix, and each of these was one reading short of it.
#
#   An INDEX is read as one. A cross-reference budget of one per hundred words is written for prose;
#   on an index the links ARE the content. docs/README.md carries 10 words and 5 links, read 50 per
#   100w, and floored Reach at zero -- instructing a writer to pad an index with prose. The card now
#   reads the page's own declaration the way declared_ceiling reads its own limit, under TWO
#   conditions, because a self-declared exemption is a door and a door beside a wall makes the wall a
#   habit: the page must DECLARE itself an index in its header (`**Depth:** routing`, `**Kind:** ...
#   index`) AND MEASURE as one, under 100 words of prose -- one full unit of the denominator the rate
#   is expressed in. Measured over every living page: four declare, three carry 13, 13, and 10 words,
#   and the fourth carries 193 and stays graded at an A.
#
#   A PLACEHOLDER SHAPE is an illustration. `date/YYYYMMDD/name` is a shape with letters standing
#   where digits go, and .claude/rules/stamp-and-name.md seats that spelling and asks for it by name.
#   construction/CHECKPOINTS.md sat at Truth 60, one point off the F gate, for writing two of them.
#   Only YYYYMMDD and HHMMSS count, the two runs that law spells inside a path shape; zero tracked
#   paths in this tree carry either literally. A FABRICATED stamp naming no file still costs twenty,
#   which is the half that keeps this a reading rather than an escape hatch.
#
#   A SHARE NEEDS A DENOMINATOR. The register scan's teaching tier has always skipped a page under
#   eight sentences -- "too short to read a share from honestly" -- and the card citing that scan
#   was dropping the floor, so one page could be unmeasurable to one reading and scored 0 by the
#   other. Measured 20260825: 27 living teaching pages sit under the floor, six of them reading
#   100% off a SINGLE sentence. The floor is now a named constant in the scan, REGISTER_MIN_SENTENCES,
#   and the card CITES it the way it already cites measure() -- losing it makes the card refuse.
#   One condition here rather than two, because a sentence count is measured rather than declared,
#   so no page can assert its way under it. The 20% wall on the twelve door documents is untouched.
#
#   A PROGRAM CITES IN ITS COMMENTS. Truth read every `](` in a file, and outside prose that pattern
#   is mostly something else: a fixture planted in a pen, a fragment of a page the file emits (whose
#   paths are relative to where the OUTPUT lands), or `x[1](32000)` arithmetic. So in a program a
#   citation is a path named on a comment line, outside backticks, that looks like a path -- and a
#   SYMLINK's citations belong to the body that wrote them. Six symlinked doors read as eleven broken
#   citations on 20260825, and repairing them would have written through the links into six correct
#   bodies. Reading the data before acting on it is what stopped that, the same way REDS %213 did.
#
# A TABLE IS NOT A PARAGRAPH, 20260831. Both counted readings are computed over SENTENCES, and a
# reference table has none: this tree writes its key lists without terminal punctuation, so a run of
# them merges into whatever sentence abuts it and the card weighs a head as if it held a handful of
# enormous ones. Twenty-eight such lines moved one real scan from C 74 to A 91 with its content
# unchanged (REDS %397). A reference block is now held out of both readings and REPORTED beside the
# prose, the way declaration docs already are, and what counts as one is read off the line's own
# face -- an entry is a bare identifier followed by two or more spaces, a continuation is indented
# past that entry's key column, and a block is two or more entries sharing one key column. TWO
# entries rather than one, because a lone double-spaced line is prose far more often than a table.
# Measured across the tree: 154 program heads carry a block, 928 lines in all, and holding them out
# moves 130 of them -- 57 across the B door, one below it, mean +7.2. Exactly one living non-dated
# prose file of 1,503 carries a block at all, so the reading is surgical rather than sweeping.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal. One hundred and seventeen behaviors in a throwaway pen -- the control's own
# yes/no readings, counted rather than recited, after this file carried 72 in one place and 79 in
# another.
# The scale at every one of its
# nine boundaries from both sides, and no minus grade anywhere. The register flip proven to BE the
# register scan's own number rather than a second measurement -- and proven load-bearing, since
# removing measure() from that scan makes the card refuse. Reach falling when a page reaches past
# its reader. Meter carrying no register or reach budget, because refusal-first prose is the subject
# there. Truth counting a link that resolves nowhere, leaving a resolving one alone, resolving a
# dated reference by the fold rule, and reading past an http link it was never able to check. The
# composite as the mean of four, and the truth gate held at 60 and bitten at 59. The card refusing
# to invent a Service it did not measure, refusing an absent path, and refusing an unknown setting.
#
# And the two new readings proven from BOTH sides. A declaring short page read as an index; a
# declaring LONG page still graded and still penalized; a short page declaring nothing still
# penalized for its link density; a declaration in the body reaching nothing. A placeholder costing nothing and
# named; a fabricated stamp still costing twenty and still named. Pointed at a copy of the card
# carrying the old rule, the control refuses 13 of those 17 and passes exactly the 4 that describe
# behavior which must NOT change -- so it is proven to bite rather than assumed to.
#
# And a program's prose is whatever ITS OWN language marks as a comment. Glow opens one with `::`,
# as do the `.brush` placards, and the extractor knew only `//` and `#` -- so 438 tracked `.glow`
# files and 8 `.brush` ones measured zero words, and all 34 residents of the shape museum graded
# C+ 75 whatever they said (REDS %358). Proven from both sides: a placard behind a mark the card
# knows is read and weighed, the same placard behind a mark it does not know reads nothing, and a
# `::` sitting mid-sentence in a `//` comment stays prose rather than becoming a second head to
# strip.
#
# AND A NOTATION'S PROSE IS ITS COMMENT BLOCK, WHILE ITS RECORDS ARE DATA. Kyri and Bron open a
# comment with `#` and close a record with nothing, so a `.kyri` read as a document lost its whole
# argument to the heading rule and read its records as ONE pseudo-sentence: 498 comment lines and
# 7,271 words dropped from `construction/standing-equipment.kyri`, 457 records read as a single
# 915-word sentence, a reading grade of 327, and the same C+ 75 the shape museum wore one family
# earlier -- nineteen notation files, one number (REDS %400). Both repairs above taught the PROGRAM
# extractor a new mark; a notation classifies as prose, where no extractor runs, so the third family
# arrived through the one door neither repair covered. Proven from both sides: two rosters with
# identical records and opposite heads that the card now tells apart and the elder card could not,
# two hundred more records moving neither the sentence count nor the grade, and the elder reading
# shown answering one sentence, which is the fault's own signature.
#
# WHICH SETTING A NOTATION TAKES, decided by grammar rather than by the typed word (20260831). The
# repair above made a roster's document readable and left the escape hatch beside it: `--setting
# meter` sets register and reach both to 100, so every one of those nineteen files read EXACTLY 94
# with Service held at 75 -- one number across nineteen different inputs, which is the disconnected
# reading the repair had just removed, available for the typing. The card now asks the file. A
# notation carrying a comment block has a document, so Meter is refused and the reading falls to
# Field, this card's own default, since Meter carries no ceiling to fall back on. A notation with no
# comment block is all record, so the free pass stands. The split is the family's, not an
# invention: measured across all 4,090 tracked `.bron` and `.kyri` files, 3,983 carry zero comment
# lines -- 3,928 session logs, which `.claude/rules/session-logs.md` already seats at Meter, plus 55
# data corpora -- and 107 carry a document. At Field the nineteen read 81 to 92, an eleven-point
# spread, every one at or above B, so the class never needed the relief. Field rather than Door
# because twelve of the nineteen exceed Door's 20% register ceiling and eight exceed its grade
# ceiling of 9; a typed `--setting door` is still honored, since whether that ceiling of 9 is right
# at all is its own open question and settling it inside this repair would be reaching.
#
# AND THE GRADE CARRIES THE FLOOR THE REGISTER READING ALREADY HELD (REDS %407, 20260831). The lap
# opened on a question: should a record-only notation DEFAULT to Meter, given that 3,928 session
# logs sit between a card grading at Field and a rule seating logs at Meter. Measurement answered a
# different one. A reading grade is two rates -- words per sentence, syllables per word -- so it
# wants a denominator exactly as a share does, and one of the card's two scored readings checked
# that denominator while the other scored on. Across 385 sampled artifacts (55 record-only notation
# files, a 60-log sample, 163 programs, all 107 documented notation files), 207 sat under the
# register scan's own eight-sentence floor and 137 of them still took a scored Reach below 100.
# Seventeen carried zero words of prose and read reach=0, the lowest point on the scale, for a page
# the card had read nothing of. A one-line module head shows it plainest:
# active-designing/docs/glow/fixtures/anchor_bad.rye printed `meter_reach=100 (0 words reported, not
# scored)` beside `reach=0 (grade 0 against 9 ... 0 words)` in one run. Data corpora show it
# largest, where the syllable heuristic counts vowel groups inside a 128-character hex string --
# mycelium/corpora/braid_dag.bron reads 6.1 syllables per word and a grade of 59 over 30 words --
# and 41 of the 55 record-only files read D+ on that alone.
#
# So the grade term takes the same cited floor, and the cross-reference term keeps the index door it
# already had. Two terms, two doors, deliberately independent: a twenty-word page with five links
# keeps its link penalty, because a rate stays a rate, while it stops being graded on a readability
# score twenty words can carry. That independence is what let this land beside a decision the index
# door made on purpose, and all four of that door's legs still pass unchanged. Session logs stand
# exactly where they stood -- 0 of 60 sat under the floor with a scored grade -- so measurement
# answers the door that sent this lap out: a record-only notation already reads correctly at Field,
# and defaulting the family to Meter would hand 3,985 files the constant the repair one row above
# had just removed.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED, as a ratchet under a ceiling that only ever falls. The twelve-document door
# roster, read as report cards, counted where the COUNTED half alone puts a page below B. One at
# seating, docs/README.md, and the ceiling fell to ZERO on 20260825 when the index reading landed --
# by measurement rather than by editing the page, which is the whole point of fixing the meter.
#
# WHAT IS NOT GATED, and why. A grade is not a gate. The register share already has its wall at
# tools/p/prose_register_witness.rish, and a second hard ceiling on the same pages would red the
# tree on readings it never agreed to hold. The card exists to aim a writer; a ratchet aims without
# refusing.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That an A page is a good page. Four honest proxies, two counted, and the
# second thing to read is always the artifact itself.
#
# Style: context/GAUGE_STYLE.md - Rule: .claude/rules/quality-assurance.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/q/qa_report_card_witness.rish

say "qa-report-card: Language EN -- a ceiling tells a writer what to avoid; a grade tells them what to reach for."
say "qa-report-card: Style Gauge -- the same measurement read the other way up, and two more beside it."
say "qa-report-card: Lens TAME -- honesty first: a page whose claims have gone false reads F whatever else it scores."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "qa-report-card: more door documents sit below B on their counted half than the ceiling allows"
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "qa-report-card: the roster reading must balance before it is believed"
say "field GREEN -- every front door read as a report card, and the ratchet holds"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "qa-report-card: the control must complete"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "scale_exact=yes" else "qa-report-card: the scale must read exactly at all nine boundaries, from both sides"
assert control.out contains "no_minus_grades=yes" else "qa-report-card: this scale carries no minus grades, by Keaton's word"
assert control.out contains "warm_register_high=yes" else "qa-report-card: affirmative prose must grade high"
assert control.out contains "cold_register_low=yes" else "qa-report-card: refusal-led prose must grade low"
assert control.out contains "register_discriminates=yes" else "qa-report-card: the register reading must tell the two apart"
assert control.out contains "register_is_the_flip=yes" else "qa-report-card: register is 100 minus the register scan's own number, never a second measurement"
assert control.out contains "register_source_load_bearing=yes" else "qa-report-card: the register reading is cited, so losing its source must refuse rather than guess"
assert control.out contains "reach_falls_on_links=yes" else "qa-report-card: a page reaching past its reader must lose reach"
assert control.out contains "reach_under_full=yes" else "qa-report-card: reach over budget must read under 100"
assert control.out contains "links_off_prose_unseen=yes" else "qa-report-card: the same ten links on a list, a table, or a bold-key header line read zero to the density budget -- the card must say so"
assert control.out contains "off_prose_links_never_cost_reach=yes" else "qa-report-card: and none of the three can cost reach, which is the consequence a reader must be able to see"
assert control.out contains "reach_links_adds_up=yes" else "qa-report-card: the whole-page count is the seen count plus the held-out one, never a third measurement"
assert control.out contains "filtered_count_reproduces_the_blindness=yes" else "qa-report-card: a whole-page count carrying the density reading own line filters reads 0 of 0 -- the elder state this report ended"
assert control.out contains "meter_register_free=yes" else "qa-report-card: Meter carries no register budget -- refusal is its subject"
assert control.out contains "meter_reach_free=yes" else "qa-report-card: Meter carries no reach budget either"
assert control.out contains "resolving_link_free=yes" else "qa-report-card: a link that lands must cost nothing"
assert control.out contains "unresolved_link_counted=yes" else "qa-report-card: a link that lands nowhere must cost twenty points"
assert control.out contains "unresolved_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: an unresolved link must be named, so it can be repaired"
assert control.out contains "fold_rule_resolves=yes" else "qa-report-card: a dated reference whose room folded is resolved, never counted as gone"
assert control.out contains "web_link_free=yes" else "qa-report-card: an http link is not a path this tree can resolve"
assert control.out contains "composite_is_mean=yes" else "qa-report-card: four hundreds must mean to a hundred"
assert control.out contains "mean_of_four_reads=yes" else "qa-report-card: the composite must be the mean of the four readings"
assert control.out contains "gate_holds_at_60=yes" else "qa-report-card: the truth gate must hold at sixty"
assert control.out contains "gate_bites_at_59=yes" else "qa-report-card: the truth gate must bite at fifty-nine, so no override exists"
assert control.out contains "gate_reads_F=yes" else "qa-report-card: a gated card reads F whatever else it scored"
assert control.out contains "service_left_judged=yes" else "qa-report-card: Service is supplied by a reader, never invented by the tool"
assert control.out contains "composite_left_judged=yes" else "qa-report-card: an unjudged card must print judged rather than a number"
assert control.out contains "service_inputs_reported=yes" else "qa-report-card: the tool must hand the judge the inputs it counted"
assert control.out contains "absent_path_refused=yes" else "qa-report-card: an absent artifact must refuse rather than read zero"
assert control.out contains "unknown_setting_refused=yes" else "qa-report-card: an unknown setting must refuse rather than default"
assert control.out contains "declared_and_short_reads_index=yes" else "qa-report-card: a page that declares an index in its header and measures under the prose floor must be read as one"
assert control.out contains "index_density_reported=yes" else "qa-report-card: an index's link density is reported rather than scored -- the links ARE its content"
assert control.out contains "index_density_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: the card must say the density was reported, so a reader sees what was read past"
assert control.out contains "declared_but_long_stays_graded=yes" else "qa-report-card: a declaring page carrying real prose stays graded -- the floor is what keeps the declaration from being an exemption"
assert control.out contains "declared_but_long_penalized=yes" else "qa-report-card: and it must actually lose reach, or the floor proves nothing"
assert control.out contains "undeclared_short_stays_graded=yes" else "qa-report-card: a short page that declares nothing stays graded -- the word count alone is no exit either"
assert control.out contains "undeclared_short_penalized=yes" else "qa-report-card: and it must actually lose reach, or the declaration proves nothing"
assert control.out contains "body_declaration_ignored=yes" else "qa-report-card: the declaration is read in the header alone, so a body discussing indexes declares nothing"
assert control.out contains "body_declaration_stays_graded=yes" else "qa-report-card: a body declaration must not reach the grade"
assert control.out contains "meter_names_its_mode=yes" else "qa-report-card: Meter names its own mode rather than borrowing either of the other two"
assert control.out contains "placeholder_costs_nothing=yes" else "qa-report-card: a placeholder shape is an illustration of a path, never a citation of one"
assert control.out contains "placeholder_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: an illustration must be named, so a reader sees what the card read past"
assert control.out contains "placeholder_counted=yes" else "qa-report-card: the card must count the illustrations it read past"
assert control.out contains "placeholder_not_cited=yes" else "qa-report-card: an illustration leaves the cited denominator, rather than resolving inside it"
assert control.out contains "hhmmss_placeholder_free=yes" else "qa-report-card: both runs the naming law spells inside a path shape are illustrations"
assert control.out contains "fabricated_stamp_still_counted=yes" else "qa-report-card: a real-looking stamp naming no file is still a broken citation -- this is the half that keeps the reading from being an escape"
assert control.out contains "fabricated_stamp_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: and it must still be named, so it can be repaired"

# A link inside a backtick span or a fenced block is not a link (seated 20260906.133800). The
# comments branch has masked code spans since it was written; prose did not, and the cost fell on
# exactly the pages that follow the mark law most carefully -- every page teaching the fold rule
# quotes `](X)` inside backticks, and each quotation cost 20 points of Truth. Measured that day: 30
# such shapes across 12 tracked pages. The mask can only REMOVE candidates, so a grade can only rise.
assert control.out contains "code_span_link_costs_nothing=yes" else "qa-report-card: a link shape quoted inside code marks is literal text, so it cites nothing and cannot be broken"
assert control.out contains "code_span_link_not_cited=yes" else "qa-report-card: a quoted shape must not even be counted as a citation, or the denominator lies"
assert control.out contains "fenced_link_costs_nothing=yes" else "qa-report-card: a link inside a fenced block is literal text too, exactly as a renderer reads it"
assert control.out contains "plain_broken_still_counted=yes" else "qa-report-card: a genuinely broken link in plain prose must still cost, or the mask is a way to stop being checked"
assert control.out contains "plain_broken_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: and it must still be named"
assert control.out contains "mixed_line_keeps_the_real_link=yes" else "qa-report-card: one line may carry a real link and a quoted shape, and the real one must survive the mask"
assert control.out contains "mixed_line_cites_once=yes" else "qa-report-card: that line cites once, so the denominator must read one"
assert control.out contains "floor_is_cited=yes" else "qa-report-card: the register floor is read out of prose_register_scan.sh, never spelled beside it"
# TWO CONDITIONS, NEVER ONE (REDS %430). Under the floor is where the argument starts. A reading is
# freed only where one sentence could still have carried the share across the ceiling -- and where
# it could not, the page pays. The elder single condition let 560 of 870 pages vote their ceiling
# from a reading that measured nothing, 206 of them printing a share above the ceiling they were
# being graded against.
assert control.out contains "under_floor_seen=yes" else "qa-report-card: the floor finding is published on its own, so both scored readings still answer the denominator question the same way"
assert control.out contains "under_floor_far_share_scored=yes" else "qa-report-card: under the floor and seventy points from the ceiling, no single sentence put it there -- it is scored"
assert control.out contains "under_floor_far_share_costs=yes" else "qa-report-card: and being scored must cost, or the amendment is a label rather than a repair"
assert control.out contains "under_floor_scored_explains=yes" else "qa-report-card: a page scored under the floor must say why, since the elder card told it the opposite"
assert control.out contains "one_sentence_under_floor=yes" else "qa-report-card: the seated case is still under the floor -- the amendment narrows the door rather than moving this case through it"
assert control.out contains "one_sentence_still_free=yes" else "qa-report-card: one negative sentence out of one is a rounding error, not a register -- the seated reasoning is kept whole"
assert control.out contains "one_sentence_not_scored=yes" else "qa-report-card: and at n=1 it must still cost nothing"
assert control.out contains "near_ceiling_still_free=yes" else "qa-report-card: under the floor and NEAR the ceiling still frees, or the rule is merely score-everything-past-one-sentence"
assert control.out contains "under_floor_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: the card must say the share was reported, so a reader still sees it"
assert control.out contains "under_floor_share_still_shown=yes" else "qa-report-card: the denominator stays visible even where the share is unscored"
assert control.out contains "at_floor_scored=yes" else "qa-report-card: a page AT the floor is scored -- the boundary is read from both sides"
assert control.out contains "at_floor_scored_low=yes" else "qa-report-card: and refusal-led prose at the floor must still grade low"
assert control.out contains "at_floor_denominator=yes" else "qa-report-card: the sentence at the floor must reach the denominator"
assert control.out contains "meter_names_register_mode=yes" else "qa-report-card: Meter names its own register mode rather than borrowing another"
assert control.out contains "floor_source_load_bearing=yes" else "qa-report-card: the floor is cited, so losing its source must refuse rather than guess"
assert control.out contains "program_cites_in_comments=yes" else "qa-report-card: in a program a citation is a path named in a comment, never a fragment of what the program emits"
assert control.out contains "program_body_truth_clean=yes" else "qa-report-card: a program whose comment citations resolve must read clean"
assert control.out contains "code_and_math_left_out=yes" else "qa-report-card: an emitted row and array-index arithmetic must both stay out of the denominator"
assert control.out contains "symlink_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: a symlink must be named, so a reader knows which of two doors was measured"
assert control.out contains "symlink_reads_the_body=yes" else "qa-report-card: a relative citation belongs to the body that wrote it, never to the door it was reached through"
assert control.out contains "body_break_seen=yes" else "qa-report-card: resolving a link is a correction, so a real break in the body must still be seen"
assert control.out contains "body_break_seen_through_door=yes" else "qa-report-card: and seen through the door as well, or the resolution is an exemption"
assert control.out contains "prose_cites_everywhere=yes" else "qa-report-card: a prose file cites everywhere -- the program rule is kept away from prose deliberately"
assert control.out contains "heading_link_still_counted=yes" else "qa-report-card: a Markdown heading begins with a comment mark, and its link must still count"
assert control.out contains "quoted_syntax_free=yes" else "qa-report-card: a page quoting link syntax inside backticks cites nothing -- the grep runs straight through a span"
assert control.out contains "quoted_syntax_not_cited=yes" else "qa-report-card: and the quoted span leaves the denominator rather than resolving inside it"
assert control.out contains "real_link_beside_quote_counted=yes" else "qa-report-card: a real broken link beside a quoted one still costs twenty -- quoting is no way to stop being read"
assert control.out contains "real_link_beside_quote_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: and it must still be named, so it can be repaired"
assert control.out contains "glow_prose_read=yes" else "qa-report-card: a Glow placard's :: prose must be read as prose"
assert control.out contains "glow_words_counted=yes" else "qa-report-card: a Glow placard must measure more than zero words"
assert control.out contains "unknown_mark_reads_nothing=yes" else "qa-report-card: the comment-mark clause must be load-bearing -- an unknown mark reads nothing"
assert control.out contains "midline_unstripped=yes" else "qa-report-card: :: mid-sentence is prose, never a second comment head"
assert control.out contains "midline_still_read=yes" else "qa-report-card: a // comment mentioning :: keeps its whole sentence"
assert control.out contains "program_setting_independent=yes" else "qa-report-card: a program's grammar chooses its settings, never the caller's word"
assert control.out contains "program_head_is_door=yes" else "qa-report-card: the module head must be read at Door"
assert control.out contains "program_bounds_are_meter=yes" else "qa-report-card: invariant bounds must be read at Meter"
assert control.out contains "program_decl_reported=yes" else "qa-report-card: declaration docs belong to neither pole and must stay visible"
assert control.out contains "program_meter_unscored=yes" else "qa-report-card: Meter bound prose is reported rather than simplified"
assert control.out contains "program_meter_cannot_lower_door=yes" else "qa-report-card: refusal-heavy bound prose must not lower the Door reading"
assert control.out contains "program_door_still_scored=yes" else "qa-report-card: a weak module head must still lower the card when the caller asks for Meter"
assert control.out contains "notation_comment_read=yes" else "qa-report-card: a notation file keeps its document behind `#`, so that block must be read rather than dropped as a heading"
assert control.out contains "notation_register_discriminates=yes" else "qa-report-card: two rosters with identical records and opposite heads must not read the same register"
assert control.out contains "notation_counts_reported=yes" else "qa-report-card: the card must name how many lines it read as document and how many it counted as data"
assert control.out contains "notation_records_are_data=yes" else "qa-report-card: two hundred more records must move neither the sentence count nor the grade"
assert control.out contains "notation_document_refuses_meter=yes" else "qa-report-card: a notation carrying a comment block has a document to read, so Meter's free pass must be refused rather than granted"
assert control.out contains "notation_refused_meter_falls_to_field=yes" else "qa-report-card: Meter carries no ceiling to fall back on, so a refused notation reads at the card's own default"
assert control.out contains "notation_meter_cannot_lift_field=yes" else "qa-report-card: the typed word must not move the reading -- the same bytes read the same letter at meter and at field"
assert control.out contains "notation_meter_refusal_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: the card must say which half of the grammar answered, rather than quietly reading something else"
assert control.out contains "notation_record_only_keeps_meter=yes" else "qa-report-card: a notation with no comment block is all record, and Meter is right for it -- a session log stays unmoved"
assert control.out contains "notation_free_pass_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: the free pass must name itself too, since a silent grant reads exactly like a silent refusal"
assert control.out contains "notation_elder_meter_was_constant=yes" else "qa-report-card: the elder meter test must be shown returning one number for two opposite rosters"
assert control.out contains "notation_meter_repair_bites=yes" else "qa-report-card: the repaired card must read a documented roster differently than the elder one, or it is a rewording"
assert control.out contains "notation_fields_still_read=yes" else "qa-report-card: a long field value is prose and stays read, whatever the comment block holds"
assert control.out contains "notation_elder_was_blind=yes" else "qa-report-card: the elder classifier must be shown unable to tell the two plants apart"
assert control.out contains "notation_elder_read_one_sentence=yes" else "qa-report-card: the elder reading must be shown answering one sentence, which is the fault's own signature"
assert control.out contains "table_leaves_prose_unmoved=yes" else "qa-report-card: one paragraph must read one grade whether or not a punctuation-free table sits beside it"
assert control.out contains "paragraph_holds_no_table=yes" else "qa-report-card: ordinary prose holds no reference block, so nothing is quietly held out of it"
assert control.out contains "table_counted=yes" else "qa-report-card: the held-out lines must be counted"
assert control.out contains "table_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: and named on the card, so a reader sees what was read past"
assert control.out contains "hold_out_load_bearing=yes" else "qa-report-card: with the block scored inside the prose the same two files must disagree -- a hold-out proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from one that does nothing"
assert control.out contains "lone_entry_stays_prose=yes" else "qa-report-card: one entry is not a block -- a lone double-spaced line is prose far more often than a table"
assert control.out contains "two_entries_make_a_block=yes" else "qa-report-card: and the second entry must make a block, or the threshold proves nothing"
assert control.out contains "continuation_rides_along=yes" else "qa-report-card: a wrapped description rides with the entry that opened it, or every wrap breaks its own run"
assert control.out contains "blank_ends_a_block=yes" else "qa-report-card: a blank line ends a block, because a blank line is how this tree ends a table"
assert control.out contains "key_column_binds_a_block=yes" else "qa-report-card: entries at different key columns are different tables, never one block"
assert control.out contains "prose_table_held_out=yes" else "qa-report-card: a prose file's reference block is read the same way a program's is"
assert control.out contains "fence_left_alone=yes" else "qa-report-card: a fenced listing is already read past, so reaching in would inflate the count and move no grade"
assert control.out contains "reference_source_load_bearing=yes" else "qa-report-card: the reference reading is cited, so losing its source must refuse rather than guess a zero"
assert control.out contains "table_leaves_prose_unmoved=yes" else "qa-report-card: one paragraph must read one grade whether or not a punctuation-free table sits beside it"
assert control.out contains "paragraph_holds_no_table=yes" else "qa-report-card: ordinary prose holds no reference block, so nothing is quietly held out of it"
assert control.out contains "table_counted=yes" else "qa-report-card: the held-out lines must be counted"
assert control.out contains "table_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: and named on the card, so a reader sees what was read past"
assert control.out contains "hold_out_load_bearing=yes" else "qa-report-card: with the block scored inside the prose the same two files must disagree -- a hold-out proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from one that does nothing"
assert control.out contains "lone_entry_stays_prose=yes" else "qa-report-card: one entry is not a block -- a lone double-spaced line is prose far more often than a table"
assert control.out contains "two_entries_make_a_block=yes" else "qa-report-card: and the second entry must make a block, or the threshold proves nothing"
assert control.out contains "continuation_rides_along=yes" else "qa-report-card: a wrapped description rides with the entry that opened it, or every wrap breaks its own run"
assert control.out contains "blank_ends_a_block=yes" else "qa-report-card: a blank line ends a block, because a blank line is how this tree ends a table"
assert control.out contains "key_column_binds_a_block=yes" else "qa-report-card: entries at different key columns are different tables, never one block"
assert control.out contains "prose_table_held_out=yes" else "qa-report-card: a prose file's reference block is read the same way a program's is"
assert control.out contains "fence_left_alone=yes" else "qa-report-card: a fenced listing is already read past, so reaching in would inflate the count and move no grade"
assert control.out contains "reference_source_load_bearing=yes" else "qa-report-card: the reference reading is cited, so losing its source must refuse rather than guess a zero"
assert control.out contains "deps_list_is_complete=yes" else "qa-report-card: a pen built from nothing but --deps must run the card, or the list has gone stale"
assert control.out contains "deps_list_is_named=yes" else "qa-report-card: --deps must name every reading the card cites, not one of them"
assert control.out contains "deps_list_resolves=yes" else "qa-report-card: every path --deps names must exist"
assert control.out contains "grade_floor_frees_the_corpus=yes" else "qa-report-card: a reading grade needs a denominator, so prose under the register scan's own floor is reported rather than scored"
assert control.out contains "grade_floor_names_the_grade=yes" else "qa-report-card: the grade must still be printed when it is not scored, the same way the register share is"
assert control.out contains "empty_prose_reads_full=yes" else "qa-report-card: a file with nothing to read cannot be unreadable -- zero words must not score zero"
assert control.out contains "floors_agree_across_readings=yes" else "qa-report-card: one card reading one prose_path must not report one scored reading and score the other"
assert control.out contains "long_prose_still_graded=yes" else "qa-report-card: prose that clears the floor is graded exactly as before, or the floor is an exemption"
assert control.out contains "link_penalty_survives_the_floor=yes" else "qa-report-card: the grade floor and the index door are separate terms -- a short undeclared page keeps its link penalty"
assert control.out contains "elder_grade_scored_the_unmeasurable=yes" else "qa-report-card: the elder card must be shown scoring a grade it had no denominator for, and an empty file at zero"
assert control.out contains "grade_floor_repair_bites=yes" else "qa-report-card: the repaired card must read the corpus and the empty file differently than the elder one, or it is a rewording"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "qa-report-card: the control must agree with itself"
# COUNTED FROM THE RUN, NEVER TYPED HERE. This line recited "one hundred and seventeen" while the
# control printed a hundred and twenty, and it had been wrong by three before this round added
# five more. A total carried inside a sentence stays at whatever it was on the day somebody typed
# it; this one is read off the pen every time (REDS %492, and the same law the crypto count guard
# holds one room over).
let proven = where (lines control.out) as l: l contains "=yes"
say "${length proven} behaviors proven in a throwaway pen, the scale read at every boundary from both sides"

# THE JUDGED READING NAMES ITS OWN SCALE (REDS %361). The composite is the mean of four readings on
# one 0-100 scale, so `--service` is 0-100 -- and that clause lived in exactly one place, the loop's
# seat prompt, while this card, the rules, and the tool's usage line all dropped it. A hand reading
# any of those answers three of four, the tool reads 3 of 100, and a page that grades A+ returns C+,
# which under the Standing block pushes a molt frame. Both branches are read, because the judged
# branch is where a hand learns what to hand in.
let scaled = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card.sh" "construction/standing-equipment.kyri" "--setting" "meter" "--service" "50"]
assert scaled.ok else "qa-report-card: the card must run on a real living path -- ${scaled.out}"
assert scaled.out contains "service_scale=0-100" else "qa-report-card: the judged reading must print its scale beside itself, never only in the arithmetic"
assert scaled.out contains "worth 25 each" else "qa-report-card: the scale must say how the four questions divide, since four is what a hand counts"

let judged = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card.sh" "construction/standing-equipment.kyri" "--setting" "meter"]
assert judged.ok else "qa-report-card: the card must run with the judged reading withheld -- ${judged.out}"
assert judged.out contains "service_scale=0-100" else "qa-report-card: the branch that asks for the judgment must name the scale it wants"
say "the judged reading carries its own scale, in both the given and the withheld branch"

say "GREEN: qa-report-card -- quality assurance, as a grade a writer can aim at."
